# The dev container's build context is the repository's root, so that the image can install the
# toolchain from `mise.toml` and `mise.lock`. Everything else in the
# checkout -- node_modules, .git, the worktrees under .claude/worktrees/ -- stays out of the context,
# which keeps the build fast and keeps the image from depending on anything the Dockerfile does not
# name. Docker reads this file, not a root .dockerignore, because its name is the Dockerfile's plus
# `.dockerignore`.
# `gh` and `git-credential-github-app` are the wrappers through which the image's `gh` and `git`
# act as the agents' GitHub App. `policy/tool-settings.json` names
# the repository the entrypoint clones into the workspace's volume at the first start.
*
!mise.toml
!mise.lock
!.devcontainer/entrypoint.sh
!.devcontainer/gh
!.devcontainer/git-credential-github-app
!policy/tool-settings.json
